## Project
**agentsmd** — First Vibe Builder Toolkit tool: agent configs, AI-assisted AGENTS.md, build conductor, capability handoffs, and OSS maintainer workflows.

## Tech stack
- Node.js (>=18)
- ESM JavaScript (zero runtime dependencies)

Package manager: `npm`

## Commands
- `run`: `node src/cli.js`
- `test`: `node --test`

## Conventions
- Before working, run `git fetch` (both Claude Code and Codex may push to this repo) and read docs/WORK_HARNESS.md, docs/OPEN_CORE_BOUNDARY.md, docs/EXTERNAL_WORKFLOW.md, and CHANGELOG.md.
- Zero runtime dependencies: use Node built-ins only (node:util parseArgs, node:fs, node:path, node:child_process).
- ESM modules; always use explicit .js extensions in relative imports.
- Single source of truth: generators read agentsmd.config.json; never hand-edit generated files.
- Each command lives in src/commands/, each output target in src/render/.
- Capability cards live in capabilities/*.json and are rendered by src/lib/capabilities.js.
- Runner handoffs may write command plans, prompts, manifests, and run summaries, but they must not execute third-party tools until a reviewed adapter exists.
- Public/private boundary is documented in docs/OPEN_CORE_BOUNDARY.md; external work should follow docs/EXTERNAL_WORKFLOW.md and the shallow checks in docs/WORK_HARNESS.md.

## Do NOT
- Do not add runtime npm dependencies without a strong, documented reason.
- Do not hard-code secrets; .mcp.json env values must use ${VAR} placeholders.
- Do not let the conductor invoke coding agents automatically until run --auto is intentionally designed and documented.
- Do not commit product strategy, private application drafts, customer notes, local run outputs, or proprietary routing logic.

## Security
- Never commit API keys or .env files.
- Recipe check commands are code the user runs: keep them transparent and minimal.
- Capability runner handoffs must keep --yes consent separate from third-party execution support.

## Tool decisions
- Before adopting a new external tool or library, run `agentsmd capabilities search "<goal>" --json` and review the matching card's risks, verification notes, and verified date.
- Treat cards marked stale as leads to re-check against the upstream source, not as current facts.

## Definition of done (review before finishing a task)
- node --test passes.
- agentsmd gen on a sample project still produces all four targets.
- New commands are documented in README.md and cli.js help.
- Work harness start/scope/boundary/verification checks are reviewed before completion.
- Public/private boundary is checked before release; private/, .agentsmd/, .env*, and tmp/ are not tracked.

## Current priorities
- Keep v0.9 focused on OSS maintainer readiness and tagged-release preparation.
- Make --ai mode reliable for Korean profile -> English AGENTS.md generation.
- Keep third-party execution disabled until a reviewed local-runner adapter is implemented and tested.
